Two cold reviews read this branch. One attacked the gate's design and returned unsound. One read the new commits and returned SHIP with no blocker.

The design attack is the important one, and its finding is not a code defect. A gate that runs inside a pull request cannot constrain that pull request: the change supplies the config that declares the policy and the command, the workflow that runs it, the script it calls, and the binary itself. Keeping the policy intact and replacing the hook command with `echo ok` passes. Recorded as issue 7cap and as zettel note hvrm.

Two fail-opens were real and are fixed here. A HEAD naming `refs/notes/reviews` made `gaff ci` synthesize an exempt ref line, so the run certified nothing and reported success. And the doc comment claiming the environment cannot reach `pull_request_head` was false for the `gaff ci` caller, which a reviewer reproduced.

The detached HEAD arm is the path every CI run takes and nothing pinned it. Tightening the new guard to cover it would have broken the gate in six repositories with a green suite.

